Bundled model code and weights
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

medmcp-cardiac vendors the CineMA segmentation model code and redistributes its
fine-tuned weights (baked into the published container image). Each remains
under its own license and carries its own citation requirements; if you use the
results in research, please cite the underlying methods (see the "Citation"
section of README.md).

  - CineMA (segment_cine_sax) — a foundation model for cine cardiac MRI; the
    ConvUNetR short-axis segmentation network and its fine-tuned weights.
    Code: MIT. https://github.com/mathpluscode/CineMA
    Weights: MIT. https://huggingface.co/mathpluscode/CineMA
    Cite: Fu et al., "CineMA: a foundation model for cine cardiac MRI",
    Communications Medicine (2026). doi:10.1038/s43856-026-01636-0

    The model code is copied verbatim (only import paths rewritten) into
    src/medmcp_cardiac/_cinema/ from the upstream commit recorded in
    src/medmcp_cardiac/_cinema/UPSTREAM; upstream's LICENSE travels with it.
    The weights are three of upstream's fine-tuned checkpoints
    (finetuned/segmentation/{mnms2,mnms,acdc}_sax, seed 0), which derive from
    the M&Ms-2, M&Ms and ACDC challenge datasets; those datasets carry their
    own citation requirements, listed in the upstream README.

  - timm (pytorch-image-models) — the Mlp, SwiGLU, DropPath, LayerScale,
    to_2tuple and use_fused_attn layers the model code imports, copied into
    src/medmcp_cardiac/_cinema/_timm.py from timm 1.0.15.
    Apache-2.0. Copyright 2020 Ross Wightman.
    https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models

